{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfhTwm6uyBUNiwxTFNrBG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"sections\":[{\"sid\":\"SEC031\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p1\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"There is no bigger scripture than this: Jesus prayed that the world would know that the Father sent him, and that the Father loved believers exactly as he loved Jesus. God loves you exactly the way he loves Jesus. If you are looking for a preaching topic, you will not find a greater one than that.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA114\",\"SRC003105\",\"SRC003106\",\"SRC003107\",\"SRC003108\",\"SRC003110\",\"SRC003111\",\"REF020\"]},{\"h\":\"p2\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Yet preachers often attach conditions to that statement that are simply not in the text. They say it is true as long as you stay right, as long as you preserve yourself, as long as you put all your heart in the Lord. They put that condition there; they made that condition. But is that what he actually said? That is not what he said in the verse. The love described is not qualified by any such clause.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA115\",\"SRC003118\",\"SRC003123\",\"SRC003124\",\"SRC003125\",\"SRC003126\",\"SRC003128\",\"SRC003134\",\"SRC003135\"]},{\"h\":\"p3\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"God knows your weakness already; your weakness is not a revelation to him. The call is to dare to believe that he loves you the same way regardless of what he already knows about you. And when you dare to believe that, you discover that the love of God is able to keep you pure. It is his goodness that brought redemption to us, not his judgment. It is his goodness, not his judgment, that produces the transformation.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA116\",\"SRC003142\",\"SRC003143\",\"SRC003144\",\"SRC003145\",\"SRC003146\",\"SRC003147\",\"SRC003148\",\"SRC003149\",\"SRC003150\",\"SRC003151\",\"SRC003152\"]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC032\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p4\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Show me one man in this Bible, just show me one person, show me one person besides Jesus who was without sin. You cannot. Every figure God used greatly carried flaws, yet God used them.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA117\",\"SRC003155\",\"SRC003158\",\"SRC003161\",\"SRC003174\",\"SRC003176\",\"SRC003177\"]},{\"h\":\"p5\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Moses is a clear case. He was so angry that he broke to pieces the stone tablets God himself had given him. Later, God became angry with Moses and told him he would not enter the promised land. A man who smashed what God had written with his own hand, and who was barred from entering the land he had led others toward, was still the man God used to lead his people.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA118\",\"EX017\",\"SRC003164\",\"SRC003167\",\"SRC003168\",\"SRC003170\",\"SRC003171\",\"SRC003172\",\"SRC003173\"]},{\"h\":\"p6\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Elijah was a sinner. In fact, according to what the Bible says, Elijah became so sick that it was the sickness that would kill him. Despite that, he remained a powerful prophet used mightily by God.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA119\",\"SRC003184\",\"SRC003185\",\"SRC003186\",\"SRC003187\"]},{\"h\":\"p7\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Look at Elisha. He had just received a double portion of Elijah's anointing. Yet the first fruit of that anointing was this: children mocked him, and he cursed them, and bears came out and killed children of Israel. That was the first recorded act flowing from his double-portion anointing.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA120\",\"EX018\",\"SRC003193\",\"SRC003194\",\"SRC003196\",\"SRC003197\",\"SRC003201\",\"SRC003202\",\"SRC003204\",\"SRC003210\",\"SRC003211\",\"SRC003212\",\"SRC003213\"],\"u\":[\"UNC011\",\"UNC012\"]},{\"h\":\"p8\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Elisha's power went further. He called things that be not as though they are. He commanded nature. He made an iron axe head float on water. He was the first man recorded to multiply bread, and Jesus was imitating him in that kind of miracle. This was the power of life carried by a flawed man.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA121\",\"EX019\",\"SRC003218\",\"SRC003219\",\"SRC003226\",\"SRC003230\",\"SRC003232\",\"SRC003234\",\"SRC003235\"],\"u\":[\"UNC011\"]},{\"h\":\"p9\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"John the Baptist is another example. He was flawed, and he lacked what New Testament believers now have, yet Jesus himself declared that you are greater than John the Baptist, because of what every believer now carries under the new covenant.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA122\",\"SRC003244\",\"SRC003250\",\"SRC003252\"]},{\"h\":\"p10\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Don't let any situation stand before you and boast against you. No. You, man of God, carry power greater than Deborah. Believers today carry more than these Old Testament figures carried, and circumstances should not be allowed to produce fear rather than the exercise of that authority.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA123\",\"SRC003257\",\"SRC003258\",\"SRC003259\",\"SRC003260\",\"SRC003261\"]}]}]}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1667,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null}